  "notes": "A compound of {連|れん} (linked, connected) and {動|どう} (movement). Functions as a noun and suru-verb.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～と{連動|れんどう}する (to be linked with ~)\n- ～に{連動|れんどう}して (in conjunction with ~)\n- {連動|れんどう}{型|がた} (interlocking type)\n- {価格|かかく}{連動|れんどう} (price linkage)\n\nUsed frequently in business and economics to describe correlated movements (e.g., prices, markets) and in technical contexts for mechanically or electronically linked systems.",
